{#
    `.. sidebar::` — the same thing as a topic, and the core renders it as an
    admonition.

    That is where it went wrong: an admonition is a warning, a note, a caution
    — something true of the reader's situation, said with a glyph that names
    which one. A sidebar is a digression with a heading, which is a topic, and
    the two are drawn alike here because they are alike.

    It does not float. In a column held to sixty-six characters there is
    nothing for it to float beside, and a box pulled out of a measure that
    narrow leaves both halves too thin to read.
#}
<aside class="sds-topic sds-panel">
    <p class="sds-topic__title">{{ renderNode(title) }}</p>
    {{ renderNode(node) }}
</aside>
